---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro'

const DESCRIPTION =
  'Rules for using the Wiracocha Labs website and its WhatsApp channel: what the channel is ' +
  'for, what we expect from you, and what you can expect from us.'
---

<LegalPage
  title="Terms of Service — Wiracocha Labs"
  description={DESCRIPTION}
  heading="Terms of Service"
  updated="November 13, 2026"
>
  <p>
    These terms cover this website and our WhatsApp channel. Using them means accepting them. If
    you do not accept them, please do not use them.
  </p>

  <h2>What the channel is for</h2>
  <p>
    Asking about our projects, our research, and the services we offer. Answers are informational.
    Nothing said in this channel is a contract, a binding quote, or professional advice — legal,
    financial, or otherwise. A price exists only when we send you a written proposal.
  </p>

  <h2>The bot</h2>
  <p>
    The WhatsApp channel is answered automatically. The bot can be wrong, incomplete, or
    out of date. Do not rely on it for urgent, irreversible, or high-stakes decisions. If you need
    a person, ask for one.
  </p>

  <h2>What we expect from you</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Do not send illegal, abusive, threatening or malicious content.</li>
    <li>Do not try to break, scrape, overload or reverse-engineer the service.</li>
    <li>Do not impersonate someone else.</li>
    <li>Do not use the channel for spam, mass messaging or automated outreach.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If you do any of this, we may stop replying or block the number, without notice or
    explanation.
  </p>

  <h2>Availability</h2>
  <p>
    We offer this channel on a best-effort basis. There is no uptime guarantee, and no obligation
    to answer. We may pause, change or shut down the channel at any time.
  </p>

