    attribution is fine; passing it off as your own is not. If you own something published here
    and want it removed, see the
    <a href="/privacy#deletion">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    This site and the channel are provided &ldquo;as is&rdquo;, without warranties of any kind. To
    the extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect or consequential damages arising
    from using them, or from not being able to use them.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of Peru. Any dispute goes to the courts of Cusco, Peru.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If something changes, we update the date at the top. The version published here is the one
    that counts.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
